# UI-MINIMAP-2: in the continuous zoom the magnifier reaches both ends of the mouse wheel's range
# (owner decisions 2026-11-17: ui_6.mp4 the furthest zoom-out, ui_7.mp4 the closest zoom-in;
# docs/re/ui.md 2.9). Its stages (magnifier_stages), closest first: the wheel's closest zoom-in
# (zoom.max_tile: zoom_ceiling, 84 * sqrt 2 = 118.794) and doublings of 84 below it (none here),
# the built levels' tile widths 84, 42, 20, then one halving per press (10, 5, 2.5, ...) while
# wider than the wheel's furthest zoom-out, then that end itself (zoom.min_tile: zoom_floor, lan5
# fitting the 1024 x 768 window, below a pixel). zoom.target, zoom.min_tile and zoom.max_tile are
# tile widths in thousandths of a pixel; zoom.at_min / zoom.at_max are 1 when the view's target is
# that end. At either end the wheel goes no further. The stepped zoom's clamp:
# ui_magnifier_range_stepped.
# Launch (--gpu: the continuous zoom needs the GPU renderer): --play data/maps/lan5.txt
# --construction-menu on --layout data/ui
resize 1024 768
wait frames 5
look 1140 516
wait frames 5
expect fact view.tile_w == 20
expect fact zoom.target == 20000
expect fact zoom.at_min == 0
expect fact zoom.at_max == 0
expect fact zoom.max_tile == 118794
# lan5 at 1024 x 768: the wheel's end lies more than three halvings past level 2, so the first
# three presses below are fixed widths.
expect fact zoom.min_tile < 2500
# The magnifier's - (826, 153), 19 x 21: one halving per press past level 2.
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.target == 10000
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.target == 5000
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.target == 2500
# On until nothing changes: more presses than stages can remain (--max-derived-levels 8 by
# default), a press at the end changes nothing. The view then targets the wheel's end exactly,
# and a wheel notch outwards changes nothing either.
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.at_min == 1
note fact zoom.target
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.target same
expect fact zoom.at_min == 1
wheel -1
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.target same
# The magnifier's + (796, 135): back through the same stages, past level 0 to the wheel's closest
# zoom-in, until nothing changes.
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
expect fact zoom.at_min == 0
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.at_max == 1
expect fact zoom.target == 118794
note fact zoom.target
click_px 805 145
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.target same
expect fact zoom.at_max == 1
wheel 1
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.target same
# And the - from there down through the built levels into the halvings again.
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.target == 84000
expect fact zoom.at_max == 0
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.target == 42000
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.target == 20000
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.target == 10000
expect fact selection.clicks == 0
expect fact camera.pans == 0
quit
